# The Phase A deployment's environment contract — `docs/08-aws-architecture.md` §3.
#
# TWO FILES, AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME FILE
# -----------------------------------------
# `.env.staging`          — read by the containers (`env_file:` in compose.prod.yml).
#                           Start from `.env.example`, override the three below.
# `.env.staging.compose`  — read by Compose ITSELF for `${...}` substitution (`--env-file`).
#                           Only the handful of values in the second block.
#
# Both are gitignored. Neither belongs in an image, a Terraform variable, or user-data — all three
# are readable by anything that can reach them.

# ── .env.staging ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything in `.env.example`, plus:
BASKFY_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://baskfy:<db-password>@postgres:5432/baskfy
BASKFY_REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379/0
BASKFY_ENVIRONMENT=staging
BASKFY_JWT_SECRET=<48+ random bytes>
BASKFY_JWT_ISSUER=baskfy
BASKFY_JWT_AUDIENCE=baskfy-web
# Root CLAUDE.md safety rail. Also baked into the image, so removing it here changes nothing —
# which is the point.
DRY_RUN=true

# ── .env.staging.compose ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BASKFY_DB_PASSWORD=<same password as in the URL above>
# BASKFY_JWT_SECRET=<same secret as above; the web container reads it through substitution>
#
# The gate. Generate BOTH with `bash tools/deploy/gate-password.sh` — it prints the plaintext once
# and `$$`-escapes the hash, which Compose requires because every bcrypt hash contains `$` and
# Compose interpolates it. A hash pasted unescaped fails every login with no useful error.
# BASKFY_GATE_USER=baskfy
# BASKFY_GATE_PASSWORD_HASH=$$2a$$14$$...
#
# BASKFY_SITE_ADDRESS=staging.baskfy.com     # a bare `:80` for local verification
# BASKFY_PUBLIC_URL=https://staging.baskfy.com
#
# Whole DIRECTIVES, not values — the Caddyfile interpolates them as lines, so an unset variable
# becomes a blank line rather than a syntax error.
# BASKFY_ACME_EMAIL_DIRECTIVE=email you@example.com
# BASKFY_ACME_CA_DIRECTIVE=acme_ca https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
#
# Image tags. Default to :local; set to the commit SHA for a real deploy, which is what makes
# rollback a tag change (runbook §6).
# BASKFY_WEB_IMAGE=baskfy-web:<sha>
# BASKFY_PY_IMAGE=baskfy-py:<sha>
#
# Host ports. 80/443 on the box; overridden only to verify on a laptop that already uses them.
# BASKFY_HTTP_PORT=80
# BASKFY_HTTPS_PORT=443
#
# On-demand revalidation secret, and it belongs in THIS file rather than `.env.staging`. The web
# service takes no `env_file:`, so `.env.staging` never reaches Next — only Compose substitution
# does. `compose.prod.yml` reads it as `${REVALIDATE_SECRET:?}`, so the stack refuses to start
# while it is unset. That is deliberate: since `2e4437e` the web middleware throws in production
# on an empty value, on every request, so the alternative to refusing is a box that serves 500
# everywhere and reports itself healthy. Any 32+ random bytes; it is compared, never displayed.
# REVALIDATE_SECRET=<32+ random bytes>

# NOT HERE, ON PURPOSE: every NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable.
# Next inlines those into the client bundle at BUILD time. Setting them here would change nothing
# while looking like it had. They are `--build-arg`s to `Dockerfile.web` (runbook §1).

# --- Google sign-in (M46; the only way in) ----------------------------------
# From the Google Cloud console, project `baskfy`, Web application OAuth client.
# Authorized redirect URIs must include:
#   https://staging.baskfy.com/api/auth/callback/google
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
# The web app needs BOTH (it runs the OAuth exchange). The API needs the CLIENT ID only, and uses
# it as the `aud` it will accept on a Google ID token — that check is what stops a token minted
# for somebody else's Google app from signing that person in, so it is not optional.
BASKFY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
BASKFY_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Build-args for the web image (not runtime). Staging must set these at `docker build`:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://staging.baskfy.com/api/v1
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://staging.baskfy.com
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_DESK_URL=https://desk.modelbasket.in   # or the staging desk, never omit
# Runtime (web container): REVALIDATE_SECRET must be non-empty in production/staging — it goes in
# the `.env.staging.compose` block above, not in `.env.staging`. Until 12 Sep 2026 this sentence
# was the whole of the instruction and nothing honoured it: the variable named here appeared in no
# compose service and in no generated env file, so there was no mechanism behind "must".
